WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.765
Welcome to Nabulines Academy.

2
00:00:02.171 --> 00:00:03.936
In this lesson, we're going to show you

3
00:00:04.005 --> 00:00:06.223
exactly how this academy is structured —

4
00:00:06.478 --> 00:00:09.323
how lessons, exercises, and projects fit

5
00:00:09.358 --> 00:00:11.447
together — so you can learn as fast as

6
00:00:11.505 --> 00:00:14.153
possible and actually build real things.

7
00:00:14.698 --> 00:00:15.743
Let's get into it.

8
00:00:15.743 --> 00:00:17.786
First, let's talk about the structure.

9
00:00:18.796 --> 00:00:21.026
This academy is organized into chapters.

10
00:00:21.374 --> 00:00:23.464
Each chapter covers one major skill or

11
00:00:23.522 --> 00:00:23.951
tool.

12
00:00:24.416 --> 00:00:26.482
Inside each chapter, you'll find lessons —

13
00:00:26.889 --> 00:00:28.874
short, focused videos like this one.

14
00:00:29.745 --> 00:00:31.671
Every lesson teaches you one specific

15
00:00:31.718 --> 00:00:32.055
thing.

16
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:33.413
One concept.

17
00:00:33.703 --> 00:00:34.319
One tool.

18
00:00:34.458 --> 00:00:35.050
One step.

19
00:00:35.398 --> 00:00:36.908
We keep them short and clear so you can

20
00:00:36.966 --> 00:00:38.823
actually finish them and move forward.

21
00:00:38.823 --> 00:00:40.437
Every lesson has three parts.

22
00:00:40.785 --> 00:00:42.759
First, the video — that's what you're

23
00:00:42.782 --> 00:00:43.583
watching right now.

24
00:00:44.222 --> 00:00:46.416
We explain the concept, show you real

25
00:00:46.462 --> 00:00:48.587
examples on screen, and walk through every

26
00:00:48.645 --> 00:00:49.017
step.

27
00:00:49.655 --> 00:00:52.511
Second, a quiz — a few quick questions to

28
00:00:52.569 --> 00:00:54.322
check that you understood the core ideas.

29
00:00:55.065 --> 00:00:58.037
And third, an exercise — a small task you

30
00:00:58.107 --> 00:00:59.755
actually do yourself to practice what you

31
00:00:59.825 --> 00:01:00.487
just learned.

32
00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:02.739
The exercise is where the real learning

33
00:01:02.797 --> 00:01:03.529
happens.

34
00:01:03.529 --> 00:01:06.339
Here's the key: don't skip the exercises.

35
00:01:07.082 --> 00:01:08.870
Watching videos feels like learning, but

36
00:01:08.951 --> 00:01:09.798
it's not enough.

37
00:01:10.344 --> 00:01:12.004
You have to type the commands, click the

38
00:01:12.039 --> 00:01:13.873
buttons, and see the results yourself.

39
00:01:14.512 --> 00:01:15.592
That's when it clicks.

40
00:01:16.137 --> 00:01:17.891
That's when you actually remember it.

41
00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:20.329
If you only watch, you'll forget

42
00:01:20.433 --> 00:01:21.420
everything in a week.

43
00:01:21.966 --> 00:01:23.847
If you do the exercises, you'll build real

44
00:01:23.893 --> 00:01:24.938
skills that stick.

45
00:01:24.938 --> 00:01:26.447
At the end of most chapters, there's a

46
00:01:26.494 --> 00:01:27.051
project.

47
00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:29.907
A project is bigger than an exercise —

48
00:01:30.778 --> 00:01:32.299
it's where you combine everything you

49
00:01:32.368 --> 00:01:33.982
learned in that chapter and build

50
00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:34.772
something real.

51
00:01:35.236 --> 00:01:36.049
Your first site.

52
00:01:36.397 --> 00:01:37.163
Your first app.

53
00:01:37.628 --> 00:01:39.381
Your first deployed page on the internet.

54
00:01:40.252 --> 00:01:41.773
Projects are your proof that you can

55
00:01:41.819 --> 00:01:42.666
actually do this.

56
00:01:42.922 --> 00:01:44.385
They're also what you'll show people when

57
00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:45.929
you say, I built this.

58
00:01:45.929 --> 00:01:47.961
Now let's talk about how to learn fast.

59
00:01:48.704 --> 00:01:51.153
The secret is consistency, not cramming.

60
00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:53.011
You don't need to spend eight hours a day

61
00:01:53.058 --> 00:01:53.626
on this.

62
00:01:53.882 --> 00:01:55.461
You need to spend a little bit of time

63
00:01:55.496 --> 00:01:56.123
regularly.

64
00:01:56.471 --> 00:01:58.723
Thirty minutes a day, five days a week —

65
00:01:58.909 --> 00:02:00.569
that's better than binging for six hours

66
00:02:00.639 --> 00:02:02.868
once and then disappearing for two weeks.

67
00:02:03.274 --> 00:02:05.027
Your brain needs repetition and time to

68
00:02:05.097 --> 00:02:06.200
absorb new ideas.

69
00:02:06.664 --> 00:02:08.603
Show up regularly, even if it's just for

70
00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:09.520
half an hour.

71
00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:11.227
Here's a simple schedule that works.

72
00:02:11.772 --> 00:02:13.340
Pick three to five days a week.

73
00:02:13.595 --> 00:02:15.604
On each of those days, watch one or two

74
00:02:15.662 --> 00:02:18.007
lessons, do the quizzes, and complete the

75
00:02:18.065 --> 00:02:18.831
exercises.

76
00:02:19.121 --> 00:02:19.632
That's it.

77
00:02:20.097 --> 00:02:21.861
If you do that, you'll finish a chapter

78
00:02:21.966 --> 00:02:22.941
every week or two.

79
00:02:23.347 --> 00:02:25.414
If you skip the exercises and just watch,

80
00:02:25.576 --> 00:02:27.446
you'll finish faster — but you won't

81
00:02:27.492 --> 00:02:28.560
actually learn anything.

82
00:02:29.431 --> 00:02:31.672
Speed without doing is just wasted time.

83
00:02:31.672 --> 00:02:33.599
When you get stuck — and you will get

84
00:02:33.646 --> 00:02:36.351
stuck, everyone does — don't just give up

85
00:02:36.397 --> 00:02:37.082
and move on.

86
00:02:37.721 --> 00:02:38.255
Pause.

87
00:02:38.998 --> 00:02:41.123
Re-watch the part you didn't understand.

88
00:02:41.866 --> 00:02:42.969
Try the step again.

89
00:02:43.712 --> 00:02:45.047
Google the error message.

90
00:02:45.209 --> 00:02:45.999
Ask Claude.

91
00:02:46.742 --> 00:02:48.831
Most problems have simple fixes, but you

92
00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:50.445
have to actually try to solve them.

93
00:02:51.316 --> 00:02:53.406
Getting unstuck is a skill, and you get

94
00:02:53.452 --> 00:02:55.403
better at it every time you practice.

95
00:02:55.403 --> 00:02:57.911
One more thing: this academy assumes

96
00:02:57.946 --> 00:02:59.176
you're starting from zero.

97
00:02:59.815 --> 00:03:01.893
We define every technical word the first

98
00:03:01.939 --> 00:03:02.857
time it appears.

99
00:03:03.402 --> 00:03:05.515
We show every click and every command.

100
00:03:06.154 --> 00:03:08.244
If something feels too basic, that's by

101
00:03:08.302 --> 00:03:10.438
design — we're making sure no one gets

102
00:03:10.496 --> 00:03:11.263
left behind.

103
00:03:12.006 --> 00:03:14.061
If something feels too fast, slow down.

104
00:03:14.699 --> 00:03:15.628
Pause the video.

105
00:03:16.034 --> 00:03:16.615
Rewind.

106
00:03:17.358 --> 00:03:18.438
Go at your own pace.

107
00:03:19.308 --> 00:03:21.317
There's no timer and no one judging you.

108
00:03:21.317 --> 00:03:22.966
Finally, remember the goal.

109
00:03:23.976 --> 00:03:25.694
You're not here to collect certificates or

110
00:03:25.764 --> 00:03:26.925
watch a hundred videos.

111
00:03:27.215 --> 00:03:28.666
You're here to build real things and

112
00:03:28.713 --> 00:03:30.338
become someone who can actually create

113
00:03:30.361 --> 00:03:30.988
with code.

114
00:03:31.731 --> 00:03:34.413
Every lesson, every exercise, every

115
00:03:34.471 --> 00:03:36.608
project — they all point toward that.

116
00:03:37.014 --> 00:03:38.790
By the end of this path, you'll have

117
00:03:38.814 --> 00:03:41.379
deployed sites, built apps, and automated

118
00:03:41.426 --> 00:03:41.995
tasks.

119
00:03:42.285 --> 00:03:44.282
You'll have a portfolio of real work.

120
00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:45.745
That's what matters.

121
00:03:45.745 --> 00:03:48.264
Alright, that's how this academy works.

122
00:03:48.903 --> 00:03:50.993
Your exercise for this lesson is simple:

123
00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:52.490
set a schedule.

124
00:03:52.897 --> 00:03:54.580
Pick which days of the week you'll learn,

125
00:03:54.685 --> 00:03:55.927
and how long you'll spend.

126
00:03:56.473 --> 00:03:58.365
Write it down or set a reminder on your

127
00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:58.806
phone.

128
00:03:59.445 --> 00:04:01.128
Consistency is everything.

129
00:04:02.312 --> 00:04:04.460
Next lesson, we're diving into what AI

130
00:04:04.518 --> 00:04:06.306
really is and why it changes everything

131
00:04:06.364 --> 00:04:07.061
for beginners.

132
00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:08.082
See you there.
